\label{.1}
 Let $e = (\Phi_q \cdot S) - |\{\Phi_q \cap \widetilde{S}\}|$. Then
$|e| \leq O(q^{d-1})$

There are canonical isomorphisms: \begin{itemize}
\item $M_q([\sigma]_D R) = R {\otimes}_D M_q(D)$
\item $M_q({\rm Spec^\sigma \, } [\sigma]_D R) = {\rm Spec \, }(R) \times _{{\rm Spec \, } D} M_q({\rm Spec \, } D)$
\item When $R$ is a graded $D$-algebra,
$M_q( {\rm Proj^\sigma \, } ([\sigma]_D R) ) = {\rm Proj \, } (R {\otimes}_{D} M_q(D))$
\end{itemize}
